  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1253 PM Wednesday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Dry weather, with near or slightly below normal \ntemperatures through the middle of next week. \n\nA sprawling area of high pressure remains in place across the Great \nLakes, Mid Atlantic, and Southeast US. Between the surface ridge to \nour north and the offshore surface low to the east of NJ, winds \nremain out of the northeast this afternoon with occasional \ngustiness. \n\nThe upper level ridge that is currently over the central CONUS will \ngradually shift east this weekend into early next week, yet the \ngreatest height rises and thickness increases associated with this \neastward shift will remain west of the mountains. The will allow for \na continued period of dry weather with sunny/mostly clear skies and \nnear or slightly below normal temperatures, lasting through at least \nthe middle of next week. The upper ridge will gradually start \nbreaking down toward the middle/latter part of next week, \npotentially opening the door to some weak moisture advection and \nincreased temperatures but until then we can expect much of the same \nweather. Daily highs in the upper 60s to lower 70s, with lows in the \nupper 30s to upper 40s.",
